                <pb facs="0215" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg157"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 5.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">GOVERNMENT AND MILITARY COMMANDANCY OF THE STATE OF
                    CHIHUAHUA—WAR SECTION NO. 39.</p>
                <p>In a communication of the 11th instant, the civil and military chief of the
                    canton of Camargo writes to this department as follows:</p>
                <p>“Persons from Atotonilco report that three hundred French burnt that place
                    yesterday, allowing families to leave. They say other places have been burned,
                    Rancho de Palomas for instance, and it is not known whether the enemy will come
                    on this way or go back.”</p>
                <p>I send this for your information and consequent action.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty!
                            <placeName>Chihuahua</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-04-14">April 14, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>LUIS TERRAZAS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister of War and Marine</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Paso del Norte</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
